<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <!--
      Privacy: ML Kit's bundled text model runs on-device, but ML Kit (com.google.mlkit:common)
      depends on Google Data Transport (com.google.android.datatransport:transport-runtime and
      transport-backend-cct), which can upload ML Kit usage/diagnostic events to Google.

      The component names below were checked against the AndroidManifest.xml inside the published
      AARs (transport-backend-cct 2.3.3, the version com.google.mlkit:common:18.11.0 requests,
      and 5.0.0): transport-backend-cct registers its uploader ("cct" backend) as this meta-data
      on the TransportBackendDiscovery service. Removing that meta-data leaves the transport
      runtime with no backend, so events are never sent. This is NOT documented by Google as an
      opt-out (there is no official ML Kit telemetry switch); it is a manifest-level workaround.

      TODO(verify on device, not done):
        1. Build the app and confirm the merged manifest
           (app/build/intermediates/merged_manifest/<variant>/.../AndroidManifest.xml) no longer
           contains "CctBackendFactory". Library-manifest removal markers apply to lower-priority
           (dependency) manifests; if it is still present, move this block into the app manifest
           (src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml).
        2. Run OCR with network capture (e.g. mitmproxy / PCAPdroid) and confirm no requests to
           firebaselogging-pa.googleapis.com / play.googleapis.com/log or similar.
        3. Re-check after every ML Kit / datatransport upgrade: new components may appear.
      The scheduler service/receiver (JobInfoSchedulerService, AlarmManagerSchedulerBroadcastReceiver)
      are intentionally left in place; removing them is not needed once no backend exists.
    -->
    <application>
        <service
            android:name="com.google.android.datatransport.runtime.backends.TransportBackendDiscovery"
            tools:node="merge">
            <meta-data
                android:name="backend:com.google.android.datatransport.cct.CctBackendFactory"
                tools:node="remove" />
        </service>
    </application>
</manifest>
